// Title: Potential DLL Sideloading Of Libcurl.DLL Via GUP.EXE
// Sigma ID: e49b5745-1064-4ac1-9a2e-f687bc2dd37e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "libcurl.dll" by the "gup.exe" process from an uncommon
//   location
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://labs.withsecure.com/publications/fin7-target-veeam-servers
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_gup_libcurl.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\gup.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\libcurl.dll") and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\Notepad++\\updater\\GUP.exe"))
